WEBVTT

01:24.060 --> 01:29.980
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

02:19.180 --> 02:21.530
And that's the dream I had.

02:25.450 --> 02:28.920
Dreams are a manifestation 
of one's deep psyche.

02:28.920 --> 02:32.080
Has something shocking
happened to you, General?

02:35.030 --> 02:36.480
Yes.

02:58.990 --> 02:59.260
Panda Collection 10

02:58.990 --> 03:01.990
<b>I Want to Be a Panda</b>

02:58.990 --> 03:01.990
[Uenono Zoo] Cute Pandas, Fluffy and Soft

02:59.260 --> 03:01.990
Panda Collection 10

03:00.820 --> 03:01.980
Oh?

03:56.680 --> 03:58.830
I think I'll make some coffee.

04:09.560 --> 04:10.560
<b>One notification</b>

04:09.560 --> 04:10.560
<b>Now</b>

04:10.680 --> 04:11.060
<b><i>An announcement from the Uenono Zoo</i></b>

04:11.270 --> 04:13.620
<i>There's been a decision
to return the pandas.</i>

04:14.360 --> 04:18.010
<i>The pandas have been a popular 
attraction for the zoo,</i>

04:18.010 --> 04:24.050
<i>so we interviewed people on the street
to see the reaction to this development.</i>

04:24.050 --> 04:26.100
<i>Here's the footage now.</i>

04:30.580 --> 04:34.110
The damage inflicted was surprisingly severe.

04:34.110 --> 04:36.950
My knees still hurt.

04:38.840 --> 04:41.620
Ah, so that's what's up.

04:41.620 --> 04:42.780
Yeah.

04:57.910 --> 05:00.110
I'm prepared now.

05:00.740 --> 05:03.570
You sure about this?

05:04.140 --> 05:05.970
Right back at you, General.

05:28.680 --> 05:30.550
What's that supposed to be?

05:36.650 --> 05:38.930
What... the...

05:43.700 --> 05:48.110
<i>He hollowed out the skin
 and closed it back up</i>

05:48.110 --> 05:52.870
<i>so it would look like a perfectly
untouched mandarin orange?!</i>

05:54.310 --> 05:56.540
You should never show your hand.

05:57.960 --> 06:00.650
And what's that <i>you've</i> made, General?

06:00.650 --> 06:02.230
A dog or something?

06:04.210 --> 06:06.620
You underestimate me.

06:11.970 --> 06:15.570
What secret plan gives you such confidence?

06:16.360 --> 06:19.300
That's right! Be afraid!

06:31.600 --> 06:32.900
A panda?!

06:34.740 --> 06:36.990
Well done, General.

06:36.990 --> 06:39.620
I'll have to get serious too.

06:41.170 --> 06:42.540
It's on!

06:43.560 --> 06:45.040
A caterpillar!

06:48.980 --> 06:50.590
A flower.

06:51.200 --> 06:53.310
I haven't lost yet.

06:54.410 --> 06:56.360
Bold words.

06:57.020 --> 06:58.050
Here goes...

07:00.800 --> 07:01.900
A turtle!

07:03.070 --> 07:04.340
An elephant!

07:04.820 --> 07:06.210
A crab!

07:06.210 --> 07:07.530
A lobster!

07:07.530 --> 07:09.110
A helicopter!

07:09.110 --> 07:11.140
What are they doing?

07:11.140 --> 07:12.100
A car!

07:12.100 --> 07:15.180
Thinking up new weaponized
 life forms, perhaps?

07:15.180 --> 07:16.570
Who can say?

07:26.350 --> 07:28.910
You're better than I expected.

07:31.040 --> 07:34.470
I get the job done when it counts.

07:42.850 --> 07:44.820
This will be the final round.

07:45.210 --> 07:46.780
Fine by me.

07:48.020 --> 07:49.600
General!

07:51.930 --> 07:54.320
Let's see it!

08:05.080 --> 08:07.200
A kotatsu monster!

08:07.950 --> 08:09.630
An Earthling!

08:10.830 --> 08:12.200
Oho.

08:12.200 --> 08:14.630
Wow, look at that!

08:14.630 --> 08:16.210
How's he standing up?!

08:16.210 --> 08:18.530
I want to make one, too!

08:18.850 --> 08:22.440
Oh, but now we're all out of oranges...

08:24.320 --> 08:26.940
I had a feeling this would happen.

08:27.650 --> 08:28.940
Don't tell me...

08:29.320 --> 08:31.150
<b>Delicious Yumeiro Mandarin Oranges</b>

08:31.790 --> 08:34.240
I bought an extra box!

08:34.240 --> 08:35.660
General!

08:36.010 --> 08:39.370
No need to thank me. However...

08:39.370 --> 08:40.370
Yeah.

08:42.090 --> 08:44.680
We'll have to eat all these.

08:45.980 --> 08:47.120
Yep.

08:52.470 --> 08:54.600
They always taste so good!

08:57.340 --> 08:58.590
Yeah.

08:59.150 --> 09:05.720
I wonder if the rest of the gang would enjoy 
it if we taught them how to make these.

09:11.530 --> 09:12.680
There.

09:15.210 --> 09:16.730
Trigger, sir.

09:16.730 --> 09:19.040
I brought the documents.

09:21.740 --> 09:23.820
What's that creature?!

09:24.130 --> 09:26.020
Oh, it's a mandarin orange.

09:26.020 --> 09:28.830
Rooney taught me how to make this.

09:33.010 --> 09:37.580
Don't teach them things 
that'll cause confusion!

09:38.010 --> 09:44.020
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

09:38.010 --> 09:44.020
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

10:00.850 --> 10:02.290
General!

10:02.290 --> 10:06.210
Wanna do that "Christmas 
present exchange" thing?

10:06.950 --> 10:08.160
Huh?

10:08.160 --> 10:13.160
Don't Earthlings do something 
like that at "Christmastime"?

10:13.160 --> 10:17.050
We <i>do</i> need to get a handle
on the Earthlings' tastes, you know.

10:13.500 --> 10:19.680
GAB

10:13.500 --> 10:19.680
GAB

10:13.500 --> 10:19.680
GAB

10:13.500 --> 10:19.680
GAB

10:13.500 --> 10:19.680
GAB

10:17.560 --> 10:19.820
Well, I've got a meeting now.

10:19.820 --> 10:21.340
We'll talk details later!

10:26.220 --> 10:27.350
What?

10:29.240 --> 10:31.160
<i>A present?</i>

10:41.060 --> 10:42.900
<i>Present...?</i>

10:47.710 --> 10:51.710
<b>Get your Christmas cake at Hope Mart</b>

10:53.140 --> 10:54.580
<i>Presen...</i>

11:03.630 --> 11:05.280
<i>Pres...</i>

11:09.230 --> 11:12.730
<b>brush</b>

11:09.230 --> 11:12.730
<b>brush</b>

11:10.530 --> 11:11.520
<i>Pre...</i>

11:25.040 --> 11:26.080
<i>Pr...</i>

11:49.080 --> 11:51.550
The secret to choosing a present?

11:51.550 --> 11:52.270
Yeah.

11:52.710 --> 11:54.850
Isn't that your specialty, old man?

11:56.380 --> 11:58.240
Let's see...

11:58.770 --> 12:03.700
Picture the recipient's smiling face
as you choose.

12:03.700 --> 12:06.260
That's what I do.

12:06.260 --> 12:07.620
Their face?

12:11.570 --> 12:14.810
The joy on their face when they see the gift.

12:14.810 --> 12:19.820
When they open it, exclaim in surprise,
 and then smile again...

12:20.260 --> 12:23.730
Ah, that makes me so happy.

12:29.700 --> 12:35.630
Do you select presents so you 
yourself can feel happy?

12:35.630 --> 12:36.600
Hmm?

12:39.850 --> 12:41.960
Well, well.

12:41.960 --> 12:45.050
You know, you might be right.

12:46.450 --> 12:49.960
Both parties receive joy.

12:49.960 --> 12:53.120
Maybe that's what gift-giving is all about.

12:58.120 --> 12:59.340
General!

12:59.340 --> 13:05.560
Hey, hey, General! Hey, hey, General!
Hey, hey, General! Hey, hey, General!

13:23.470 --> 13:24.880
Now I get it.

13:42.260 --> 13:44.000
So, General...

13:44.550 --> 13:46.520
Are you sure you're ready?

13:48.650 --> 13:51.530
Who do you think you're talking to?

13:52.710 --> 13:54.620
I'd expect no less from you.

13:54.620 --> 13:57.090
Now, let's get this over with.

14:01.260 --> 14:03.100
Merry Christmas!

14:03.320 --> 14:03.690
<b>Mandarins</b>

14:27.480 --> 14:29.600
Perhaps we're <i>too</i> like-minded?

14:29.970 --> 14:31.970
I'll never live this down.

14:31.970 --> 14:34.360
You say that now,

14:34.360 --> 14:36.540
but let's do this again next year!

14:36.540 --> 14:39.270
We can get <i>all</i> the higher-ups to take part.

14:39.590 --> 14:40.450
Huh?

14:42.820 --> 14:44.530
Not bad.

14:45.930 --> 14:47.540
Tasty, right?

14:48.100 --> 14:53.350
But there are so many of them, 
we should share with everyone.

14:57.060 --> 14:58.590
You guys!

14:58.590 --> 15:00.670
We have mandarins in the control room!

15:00.670 --> 15:02.290
Help yourselves!

15:02.290 --> 15:03.450
Sweet!

15:02.810 --> 15:04.510
Thank you, sir!

15:08.530 --> 15:10.350
Where'd you get those?

15:10.350 --> 15:12.340
The control room.

15:14.100 --> 15:15.790
Here, you can have one.

15:15.790 --> 15:17.640
Really? You sure?

15:18.190 --> 15:20.700
What do they have now?

15:22.610 --> 15:24.610
Hey, Rooney!

15:26.280 --> 15:27.520
Yeah?

15:28.770 --> 15:33.280
Sorry, Trigger. We just ran out.

15:33.280 --> 15:34.410
Huh?

15:42.740 --> 15:45.030
You'll have to settle for this.

15:48.210 --> 15:49.930
It's milk flavored.

15:51.830 --> 15:53.430
Well, I don't want it!

16:47.420 --> 16:48.490
Sora.

16:48.490 --> 16:50.770
Sora, wake up.

16:59.390 --> 17:00.990
Hey, Sora.

17:00.990 --> 17:02.640
There are presents.

17:13.680 --> 17:15.090
You're right.

17:15.090 --> 17:16.570
They were just there.

17:17.390 --> 17:19.350
Can we open them now?

17:19.350 --> 17:21.760
But it's still dark outside.

17:26.850 --> 17:30.300
We'll wait until it's
a little lighter out, then.

17:30.300 --> 17:32.940
Yeah, just a little longer.

17:44.510 --> 17:46.470
This is the one I wanted.

17:48.060 --> 17:49.400
Black.

17:50.820 --> 17:52.330
Why did I get one, too?

17:52.330 --> 17:54.760
I'm in my twenties, you know.

18:00.310 --> 18:03.830
From Santa's point of view,
 we never grow up.

18:05.720 --> 18:06.760
Huh?

18:32.040 --> 18:38.050
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

18:32.040 --> 18:38.050
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

18:45.350 --> 18:47.350
Let us begin the meeting.

18:53.320 --> 18:55.360
The topic is befriending pandas,

18:55.360 --> 18:58.990
which we'll proliferate 
after humanity is exterminated.

18:59.960 --> 19:01.240
Objection.

19:01.240 --> 19:04.330
Yes, the me who likes white bears?

19:04.840 --> 19:07.550
While calling them "white bears" is charming,

19:07.550 --> 19:10.190
I prefer to call the name polar bears.

19:10.190 --> 19:11.790
Call them whatever you like.

19:12.210 --> 19:19.670
I recommend we proliferate polar bears 
after humanity's downfall, not pandas.

19:21.250 --> 19:22.270
Objection!

19:22.270 --> 19:23.730
Objection.

19:23.730 --> 19:26.060
Yes, the me who likes red pandas

19:26.060 --> 19:28.200
and the me who likes grizzlies?

19:28.610 --> 19:33.930
Since white bear me already went there,
I say it's red pandas we should increase!

19:30.420 --> 19:32.180
Polar bear!

19:33.930 --> 19:37.080
Behold this lovable form!

19:37.080 --> 19:38.150
No!

19:38.150 --> 19:40.580
I endorse the grizzly!

19:41.780 --> 19:45.090
Their strength will be 
an asset to our home world!

19:45.480 --> 19:49.580
They're cool <i>and</i> cute! 
The strongest of them all!

19:50.480 --> 19:52.140
Just a moment.

19:52.140 --> 19:54.210
Yes, the me who likes teddy bears?

19:54.840 --> 19:57.330
For the most part, 
we collectively like bears.

19:57.330 --> 20:00.730
Let's make them all into teddies
and decorate with them.

20:01.140 --> 20:03.340
I don't know what you're talking about!

20:01.880 --> 20:02.660
Be quiet!

20:02.660 --> 20:03.510
Get real!

20:03.340 --> 20:06.710
The red panda isn't in the Ursidae 
family! It's an Ailuridae!

20:03.710 --> 20:05.920
We're talking about living things here!

20:07.010 --> 20:08.710
May I speak too?

20:08.710 --> 20:10.730
Yes, the me who likes Chinese buns?

20:10.730 --> 20:12.230
I taste great!

20:12.230 --> 20:16.090
Chinese buns are enjoyed both 
for their flavor and adorable shape.

20:16.090 --> 20:21.700
We should take over a production line 
so we can still eat them post-humanity.

20:21.700 --> 20:22.890
I approve.

20:22.210 --> 20:23.380
Seconded!

20:22.750 --> 20:23.820
Well said!

20:23.310 --> 20:24.660
Seconded!

20:23.700 --> 20:24.710
Agreed!

20:24.710 --> 20:25.790
Seconded.

20:25.480 --> 20:27.710
Well played, me who likes Chinese buns.

20:26.380 --> 20:27.710
Seconded!

20:27.710 --> 20:29.280
I'd like to speak, too!

20:28.520 --> 20:29.400
Me, too!

20:28.900 --> 20:29.970
And me!

20:29.050 --> 20:30.970
I want to be heard as well.

20:30.970 --> 20:32.420
We should go with rabbits!

20:32.420 --> 20:35.210
Wait! First we need to talk about dogs!

20:32.620 --> 20:34.090
Badgers aren't bad, either.

20:34.090 --> 20:35.620
Those are in Mustelidae!

20:34.480 --> 20:36.270
Listen to me first!

20:35.520 --> 20:37.430
Ferrets are uncommonly cute, too!

20:36.100 --> 20:38.240
What about kangaroos?!

20:38.240 --> 20:39.270
What about squirrels?

20:39.270 --> 20:40.960
Sun bears are awesome, too!

20:39.620 --> 20:41.690
Listen to what I'm saying!

20:40.950 --> 20:43.510
I say we spread sweet potato soft serve.

20:43.510 --> 20:45.180
I'm of the same opinion.

20:43.510 --> 20:47.180
Then I say we make the winter-exclusive
strawberry mochi bar year-round.

20:45.180 --> 20:46.350
I second that.

20:47.110 --> 20:48.640
Makes sense to me.

20:49.520 --> 20:51.670
This is getting us nowhere.

20:52.220 --> 20:55.050
You guys are so noisy.

21:00.590 --> 21:03.060
The me who likes cats!

21:03.620 --> 21:10.270
Today, I'm gonna school you 
on the appeal of cats.

21:10.830 --> 21:12.180
Say what?!

21:11.470 --> 21:12.560
Be quiet!

21:12.560 --> 21:13.720
Don't do it!

21:13.720 --> 21:14.650
Shut up!

21:13.720 --> 21:16.500
All of us here already know all about that!

21:14.650 --> 21:16.500
You dastardly villain!

21:17.800 --> 21:20.160
So, about cats...

21:19.290 --> 21:22.000
S-Stop!

21:39.520 --> 21:45.280
<b>rub...</b>

23:20.080 --> 23:20.790
MR. VILLAIN'S DAY OFF

23:20.080 --> 23:20.790
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

23:21.620 --> 23:23.910
A cat's young: a kitten.

23:24.460 --> 23:26.710
A lion's young: a cub.

23:28.130 --> 23:32.060
Toyed with by a devil and an angel.

23:32.060 --> 23:34.350
Nailed by a beanshooter.

23:34.350 --> 23:36.440
Even ogres cry.

23:40.230 --> 23:43.400
The answer is in the wind.

23:44.830 --> 23:46.690
The way of desire.

23:48.740 --> 23:50.020
The Way of Desire
